          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Massey product
            of length
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is a certain
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+ring"} cohomology ring
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+algebra"} A-infinity algebra
            (in particular a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
          %h3#in_components In components
          %p
            Roughly, Massey Products are to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toda+Brackets"} Toda Brackets
            are to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
          %p
            Somewhat more fully, while Toda brackets are relations between mapping space groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Map
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Map_* (\Sigma^n A_0, A_{n+2})
            and chains of maps
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_0 \to \cdots \to A_{n+2}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 0
                      %mo +
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{p_0 + \cdots + p_k - k + 1}(X)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{p_0} (X) \otimes \cdots \otimes H^{p_k}(X)
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cup+product"} cup product
          %p
            The case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k=2
            is straight-forward enough: given three homogeneous classes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [u],[v],[w]
            such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⌣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⌣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [u]\smile[v] = [v]\smile[w] = 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s , t
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi s
                  %mo =
                  %mi u
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d s = u \cdot v
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi t
                    %mo =
                    %mi v
