          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToSteenrodSquares Relation to Steenrod squares
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega, \omega_1, \omega_2 \in H^\bullet(X,\mathbb{Z}/2)
            such that their triple Massey product exists. Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cup+product"} cup product
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            with the triple Massey product is independent of the ambiguity in the Massey products and equals the cup product of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_2
            and with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steenrod+square"} Steenrod square
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            of degree
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} deg(\omega)-1
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∪
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⟩
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∪
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∪
                  %msup
                    %mi Sq
                    %mrow
                      %mi deg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega \cup
                  \\left\langle
                  \\omega_1, \omega, \omega_2
                  \\right\rangle
                  \\;=\;
                  \\omega_1 \cup \omega_2 \cup Sq^{ deg(\omega) -1 }( \omega )
                  \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Taylor11"}> Taylor 11, slide 10
            , following
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Milgram68"} Milgram 68
          %h3#RelationToAInfinityAlgebras
            Relation to
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_\bullet(A)
            inherits an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+algebra"} A-infinity algebra
            structure by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kadeishvili%27s+theorem"} Kadeishvili's theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            the
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-product" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1, \cdots, a_n) \in H_\bullet(A)^n
            is
            %em often
            given, up to a sign, by the Massey product
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle a_1, \cdots, a_n\rangle
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 3
            this is due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Stasheff"} Stasheff
            = succeed "-products" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            the situation is discussed in
            %a{:href => "#BMM20"} BMM 2020
            (where it is also shown that the earlier claim in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#LPWZ"} LPWZ, theorem 3.1
            = succeed "-products" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
