          %h3#ReferencesRelationToAInfinity
            Relation to
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
          %p
            On the relation of Massey products to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+algebra"} A-infinity algebra
            structures, for
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 3
          %ul
            %li#Stasheff
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"}> Jim Stasheff
              , Chapter 12 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em H-spaces from a homotopy point of view
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 161
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0065896"} doi:10.1007/BFb0065896
          %p
            A statement for higher
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            was claimed in
          %ul
            %li#LPWZ
              D.-M. Lu, J. H. Palmieri, Q.-S. Wu, J. J. Zhang, Theorem 3.1 and Corollary A.5 of,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
                  \-structures in Ext algebras
              %strong 213
              (2009) 2017–2037 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0606144"}> arXiv:math/0606144
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p but the situation is more subtle, as explained in:
          %ul
            %li#BMM20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urtzi+Buijs"}> Urtzi Buijs
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Manuel+Moreno-Fern%C3%A1ndez"} José Manuel Moreno-Fernández
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aniceto+Murillo"} Aniceto Murillo
              = succeed "," do
                %em A-infinity structures and Massey products
              %strong 17
              31 (2020) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.03408"}> arXiv:1801.03408
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00009-019-1464-1"} doi:10.1007/s00009-019-1464-1
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruno+Vallette"}> Bruno Vallette
                , item 1.4 in:
                %em Algebra+Homotopy=Operad
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1202.3245"}> arXiv:1202.3245
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#ValetteLoday
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruno+Vallette"}> Bruno Vallette
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Loday"} Jean-Louis Loday
                %em Algebraic Operads
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://math.unice.fr/~brunov/Operads.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Notice that the definition of Massey product on top of p.282 of
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ValetteLoday"} Vallette-Loday
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle x,y,z\rangle
            depends on choices of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b
            which don’t appear in the notation. Then lemma 9.4.11 talks about a particular choice of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b
            which is made in the body of the proof. The actual statement of the lemma only can be deduced after reading the proof. It then says that for these particular choices of a,b the said equality holds. (See
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/92315/massey-products-vs-a-infty-structures"} this MO discussion
